  "caption": "Quinn's finger started clicking with every text, and some mornings it was stuck bent like a hook. Quinn's plan was to keep snapping it through. Not a great plan.\n\nA finger that clicks or locks often comes from an irritated tendon catching in its pulley. It's common over 40 and it isn't arthritis.\n\nWhat often helps: cut back repetitive or tight gripping, wear a night splint that keeps the finger straight, move it gently without forcing the click, and give splinting several weeks. If you have diabetes, let your GP know.\n\nGet it checked if the locking keeps happening or the finger gets stuck bent.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
